{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 149,
    "dDurationMs": 2681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Does the Universe Have a Purpose?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2830,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm not sure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4770,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyone who expresses a more definitive response\nto the question is claiming access to knowledge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9730,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not based on empirical foundations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12280,
    "dDurationMs": 4729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This remarkably persistent way of thinking,\ncommon to most religions and some branches"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17009,
    "dDurationMs": 6121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of philosophy, has failed badly in past efforts\nto understand, and thereby predict the operations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23130,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the universe and our place within it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25550,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To assert that the universe has a purpose\nimplies a desired outcome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29310,
    "dDurationMs": 1610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But who would do the desiring?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30920,
    "dDurationMs": 2350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what would a desired outcome be?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33270,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That carbon-based life is inevitable?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35070,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or that sentient primates are life's neurological\npinnacle?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38370,
    "dDurationMs": 8320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course humans were not around to ask these\nquestions for 99.9999% of cosmic history."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46690,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if the purpose of the universe was to create\nhumans then the cosmos was embarrassingly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51300,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inefficient about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53010,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if a further purpose of the universe was\nto create a fertile cradle for life, then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57290,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our cosmic environment has got an odd way\nof showing it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60530,
    "dDurationMs": 5050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Life on Earth, during more than 3.5 billion\nyears of existence, has been persistently"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65580,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assaulted by natural sources of mayhem, death,\nand destruction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70700,
    "dDurationMs": 5150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ecological devastation exacted by volcanoes,\nclimate change, earthquakes, tsunamis, storms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75850,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and especially killer asteroids have left\nextinct 99.9% of all species that have ever"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82010,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lived here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83010,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How about human life itself?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84930,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you are religious, you might declare that\nthe purpose of life is to serve God."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89380,
    "dDurationMs": 4529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you’re one of the 100 billion bacteria\nliving and working in a single centimeter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93909,
    "dDurationMs": 4241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of your lower intestine, you might instead\nsay that the purpose of human life is to provide"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98150,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you with a dark, but idyllic, anaerobic habitat\nof fecal matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102760,
    "dDurationMs": 4469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in the absence of human hubris, the universe\nlooks more and more random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107229,
    "dDurationMs": 4151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whenever events that are purported to occur\nin our best interest are as numerous as other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111380,
    "dDurationMs": 5370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "events that would just as soon kill us, then\nintent is hard, if not impossible, to assert."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116750,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So while I cannot claim to know for sure whether\nor not the universe has a purpose, the case"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121490,
    "dDurationMs": 5559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "against it is strong, and visible to anyone\nwho sees the universe as it is rather than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127049,
    "dDurationMs": 2291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as they wish it to be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129340,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm Neil deGrasse Tyson."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131920,
    "dDurationMs": 7269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I was asked by The Templeton Foundation to\nrespond to a question: Does the Universe Have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139189,
    "dDurationMs": 561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a Purpose?"
    } ]
  } ]
}
